  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Preheat the oven to 200C. Line an oven tray with baking paper. Thinly slice the capsicum and onion. Cut the haloumi into 1cm-thick strips. Put 2 tsp fennel seeds (see Make it yours) and 2 tsp olive oil in a large bowl. Add the capsicum, onion and haloumi and toss to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/144684/photos/large/prep_ingredients-aa15c073e3c08176974a1da9218092d0.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Roast veggies and haloumi: Put the haloumi mixture on the lined tray and season with salt and pepper. Roast for 15-18 mins, turning halfway, until the haloumi is golden and the vegetables are tender.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/144685/photos/large/roast_veggies_and_haloumi-a67d3c9cd38aea9441853440153877b5.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Warm wraps: Enclose the wraps in baking paper, then foil. Put in the oven for 8 mins or until softened and warmed through.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/144686/photos/large/warm_wraps-60c9e56f2dc96084c44da6737724e05a.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make parsley salsa: Meanwhile, coarsely chop the parsley, discarding the stems. Put the parsley, 2 tsp red wine vinegar and 2 tsp olive oil in a bowl, season with salt and pepper and stir to combine. Crush 1 garlic clove. Put the yoghurt and garlic in a bowl and stir to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/144687/photos/large/make_salad_and_dressing-34c623e8c5c65fd0c2d6f92d3c0be6fc.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Spread the wraps with the garlic yoghurt. Divide the haloumi mixture and parsley salsa among the wraps and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/144688/photos/large/serve_up-49e5910f38fc1623b1d5a18d6df42e34.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it yours: If there are people in your family who aren't fans of fennel, you can toss half the haloumi and vegetable mixture in the fennel seeds and leave the other half plain. Roast on a separate tray, rotating trays halfway.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/144689/photos/large/kitchen_tip-f5c01ff72a4d69d60052772e81461c13.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
